    "introduction": "Bunzl distributes everyday operating supplies that businesses need but generally do not manufacture themselves. Products include food packaging, cleaning materials, safety equipment and healthcare consumables for customers such as retailers, caterers, hospitals and industrial companies. It earns revenue by sourcing products from suppliers and delivering them through specialised distribution businesses. Customers can simplify purchasing by obtaining multiple essential items through one relationship, with service reliability and availability supporting repeat orders. Its model depends on procurement, inventory management and efficient logistics. Growth comes from existing customer activity and acquisitions, while input-price changes, product mix and the cost of serving customers affect distribution margins.",
